{"type":"text","timestamp":1794310867809,"sessionID":"ses_e3ac69c15ffeWLjU8hG7i6xm3D","part":{"id":"prt_1c5429eac001OdjWmz2qGL8g9N","sessionID":"ses_e3ac69c15ffeWLjU8hG7i6xm3D","messageID":"msg_1c5428e76001d6iL7o2Fl6ZFVh","type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n**`todo/model.py`** — Added `priority: str = \"normal\"` field to the `Task` dataclass.\n\n**`todo/store.py`** — \n- `load()`: Detects whether the file is a bare JSON list (old format) or a `{\"version\": 2, \"tasks\": [...]}` object. For old-format lists, tasks get `priority = \"normal\"`. Any other version raises `ValueError`.\n- `save()`: Always writes version 2 format.\n\n**`todo/cli.py`** —\n- `add` subcommand: Added `--priority` option with choices `low|normal|high`, defaulting to `normal`. Invalid values cause argparse to exit with status 2.\n- `list` subcommand: Added `--sort priority` option. When set, tasks are sorted by priority (high → normal → low), then by ascending id within each priority tier. Without it, tasks remain sorted by id.\n- Output format: Non-normal tasks get ` (priority)` appended, e.g. `1 [ ] Buy milk (high)`. Normal-priority tasks are shown without suffix.","time":{"start":1794310839980,"end":1794310867809}}}
